`Onyx.multiSet(onyxSetParams)` is called without chaining its returned promise. The subsequent `Onyx.set()` calls, `confirmReadyToOpenApp()`, and `openApp()` execute immediately without waiting for `multiSet` to complete. This creates a race condition where the app may attempt to open before the stashed session data (credentials and session) has been written to Onyx, potentially causing authentication failures or the login page flash this PR aims to fix.

The existing supportal branch at line 428 correctly chains the promise: `Onyx.multiSet(onyxSetParams).then(() => { ... })`. The new branch should follow the same pattern.

Chain the `Onyx.multiSet` promise and move all dependent operations inside the `.then()` callback:

```ts
Onyx.clear(KEYS_TO_PRESERVE_SUPPORTAL).then(() => {
    Onyx.multiSet(onyxSetParams).then(() => {
        Onyx.set(ONYXKEYS.STASHED_CREDENTIALS, {});
        Onyx.set(ONYXKEYS.STASHED_SESSION, {});

        confirmReadyToOpenApp();
        openApp();

        if (CONFIG.IS_HYBRID_APP && hasSwitchedAccountInHybridMode) {
            HybridAppModule.switchAccount({
                newDotCurrentAccountEmail: stashedSession.email ?? '',
                authToken: stashedSession.authToken ?? '',
                policyID: '',
                accountID: '',
            });
        }
    });
});
```

