The callback was changed from synchronous (fire-and-forget) to `async` with `await completeOnboarding(...)`, but there is no try/catch around this critical API call. If the request fails, the subsequent `setOnboardingAdminsChatReportID()`, `setOnboardingPolicyID()`, and `navigateAfterOnboardingWithMicrotaskQueue()` calls will never execute, silently leaving the user stuck in the onboarding flow.

Note that `BaseOnboardingInterestedFeatures.tsx` already wraps the same `await completeOnboarding(...)` call in a try/catch with `Log.warn`. Apply the same pattern here:

```ts
try {
    const response = await completeOnboarding({...});
    const rhpVariant = extractRHPVariantFromResponse(response);
    setOnboardingAdminsChatReportID();
    setOnboardingPolicyID();
    navigateAfterOnboardingWithMicrotaskQueue(...);
} catch (error) {
    Log.warn('[useAutoCreateTrackWorkspace] Error completing onboarding', {error});
}
```

