The `Promise.all` chain includes critical operations (`openApp`, `waitForIdle`) but has no `.catch()` handler. If any promise in the chain rejects, the error goes unhandled and `Navigation.dismissModal()` will never be called, leaving the user permanently stuck on the sign-in modal with no way to proceed.

Add a `.catch()` handler to log the error and still attempt to dismiss the modal so the user is not trapped:

```tsx
Promise.all([
    waitForIdle()
        .then(() => openApp(true))
        .then(() => waitForIdle()),
    Navigation.isNavigationReady(),
]).then(() => {
    Navigation.dismissModal();
}).catch((error) => {
    Log.alert('Failed to complete sign-in flow', {error});
    Navigation.dismissModal();
});
```

