The `loadPostSplashScreenModules` function fires four dynamic `import()` calls that each return a promise, but none of them have `.catch()` handlers or are wrapped in a try/catch. If any of these module loads fail (e.g., bundler issue, missing chunk), the promise rejects silently and the corresponding feature (push notifications, unread indicator updates, pagination config, or optimistic report replacement) will be broken with no diagnostic information.

Add error handling to each `import()` call so failures are logged:

```tsx
function loadPostSplashScreenModules() {
    import('./libs/actions/replaceOptimisticReportWithActualReport').catch((e) => Log.alert('Failed to load replaceOptimisticReportWithActualReport', e));
    import('./libs/Notification/PushNotification/subscribeToPushNotifications').catch((e) => Log.alert('Failed to load subscribeToPushNotifications', e));
    import('./libs/registerPaginationConfig').catch((e) => Log.alert('Failed to load registerPaginationConfig', e));
    import('./libs/UnreadIndicatorUpdater').catch((e) => Log.alert('Failed to load UnreadIndicatorUpdater', e));
}
```

