`Promise.all(filePromises).then(...)` for Google Docs images has no `.catch()` handler. If any `fetch(image.src)` call fails (network error, CORS, etc.), the entire `Promise.all` rejects unhandled. Since `return true` on the next line already executed synchronously, the caller believes the paste was handled, but `pasteValidFiles()` never runs and the pasted images are silently lost.

Add a `.catch()` so that failures still attempt to paste whatever files were already collected:
```typescript
Promise.all(filePromises)
    .then((f) => {
        files.push(...f.filter((file) => file !== undefined));
    })
    .catch(() => {
        // Individual fetch failures should not block other collected files
    })
    .finally(() => {
        pasteValidFiles();
    });
```

