`Promise.all` rejects as soon as any single inner promise rejects. If `getFileSize` fails for one pasted file, the `.then()` branch never runs and `files` stays `[]`. The `.catch()` logs a warning but then `.finally()` calls `onPasteFile([])`, silently dropping every file the user pasted.

Use `Promise.allSettled` so that individual file-size failures do not discard successfully resolved files:
```typescript
Promise.allSettled(filePromises)
    .then((results) => {
        files = results
            .filter((r): r is PromiseFulfilledResult<FileObject | undefined> => r.status === 'fulfilled')
            .map((r) => r.value)
            .filter((file): file is FileObject => file !== undefined);
    })
    .finally(() => {
        onPasteFile(files);
    });
```

