The `Promise.all(filePromises)` chain for Google Docs images uses `.then()` without a `.catch()` handler. If any `fetch(image.src)` call fails (e.g., network error, CORS issue), the promise rejection will be unhandled, potentially crashing the app or silently losing the error.

Add a `.catch()` handler to log the error and gracefully handle the failure:

```typescript
Promise.all(filePromises)
    .then((f) => {
        files.push(...f.filter((file) => file !== undefined));
        pasteValidFiles();
    })
    .catch((error) => {
        Log.warn('Google Doc images could not be fetched', {error});
    });
```

